{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"subscript","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"R","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"r","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SlsEy11SubSequenceQzqd__cSXRd__5BoundQyd__5IndexRtzluip1RL_qd__mfp","text":"R","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Collection\/SubSequence","text":"SubSequence","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl11SubSequenceQa"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"R","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/RangeExpression","text":"RangeExpression","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SX"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Collection\/Index","text":"Index","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa"},{"text":" == ","kind":"text"},{"text":"R","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/RangeExpression\/Bound","text":"Bound","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SX5BoundQa"},{"text":" { ","kind":"text"},{"text":"get","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" }","kind":"text"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The range expression is converted to a concrete subrange relative to this"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"collection. For example, using a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PartialRangeFrom"},{"type":"text","text":" range expression"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with an array accesses the subrange from the start of the range"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"expression until the end of the array."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let streets = [\"Adams\", \"Bryant\", \"Channing\", \"Douglas\", \"Evarts\"]","let streetsSlice = streets[2...]","print(streetsSlice)","\/\/ [\"Channing\", \"Douglas\", \"Evarts\"]"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The accessed slice uses the same indices for the same elements as the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"original collection uses. This example searches "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"streetsSlice"},{"type":"text","text":" for one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of the strings in the slice, and then uses that index in the original"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"array."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let index = streetsSlice.firstIndex(of: \"Evarts\")    \/\/ 4","print(streets[index!])","\/\/ \"Evarts\""],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Always use the slice’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"startIndex"},{"type":"text","text":" property instead of assuming that its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"indices start at a particular value. Attempting to access an element by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"using an index outside the bounds of the slice’s indices may result in a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"runtime error, even if that index is valid for the original collection."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["print(streetsSlice.startIndex)","\/\/ 2","print(streetsSlice[2])","\/\/ \"Channing\"","","print(streetsSlice[0])","\/\/ error: Index out of bounds"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"style":"note","type":"aside","name":"Complexity","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O(1)"}]}]}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swi